title: AfterInteractedWithItems
position: 315,-648
---
<<fade_transition 2>>
<<wait 1>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<hide_ui ClickToInteract>>
<<show Stars>>
<<show Sitting>>
This is the life that I've committed myself to, ever since taking the job to pilot this small exploration vessel.
Earth launched an initiative to find out why the sun suddenly had a hole in the center... a dark spot that appeared one day and never went away. It's a three-year journey just to get there. I'm on the seventh expedition they've sent.
My dad was the pilot of the last one.
Dad... I hope I can find you out here.
But deep inside, I knew signing up was just to get a chance away from Earth.
<<jump HearRadioSignals>>
===

title: HearRadioSignals
position: 315,-550
---
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show PCRoom>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
<<play_sound Glitch 0.25>>
The communication panel pings, sharp and insistent. Locked onto a frequency I didn't dial in.
Three new packets sit in the buffer, tagged with an unknown sequence.
The ship's translator does what it can. It renders the signals into clipped, robotic phonemes.
It isn't a sentence. It's a pulse. A test pattern that learned three words.
<<speed 0.4>>
<<play_sound RobotTest 0.25>>
"TEST" <i>[79 DAYS AGO]</i>
<<play_sound RobotHello 0.25>>
"HELLO" <i>[41 DAYS AGO]</i>
<<play_sound RobotTalk 0.25>>
"TALK" <i>[5 DAYS AGO]</i>
<<speed 1>>
My fingers hover over the response key. I don't know what to make of this.
    -> (send a ping back)
        <<jump SentPingDay1>>
    -> (ignore it)
        I tell myself it's probably just interference. Cosmic noise. Nothing to worry about.
        The ping repeats anyway. Patient. Persistent.
        <<speed 0.4>>
        <<play_sound RobotTest 0.25>>
        "TEST" <i>[79 DAYS AGO]</i>
        <<play_sound RobotHello 0.25>>
        "HELLO" <i>[41 DAYS AGO]</i>
        <<play_sound RobotTalk 0.25>>
        "TALK" <i>[5 DAYS AGO]</i>
        <<speed 1>>
        It's as if it's waiting for me.
            -> (send a ping back)
                <<jump SentPingDay1>>
            -> (ignore it again)
                I shake my head and turn away from the monitor. Whatever it is, it can wait.
                <<jump RegularTasksDay1>>
===

title: SentPingDay1
position: 315,-500
---
I press the response key and send a ping back down the line.
As a one-way signal, there's no way to tell what's waiting on the other side. I can only hope the other side taps back.
Either way, my routine is still here.
    -> (try to act normal)
        <<jump RegularTasksDay1>>
===

title: RegularTasksDay1
position: 315,-500
---
<<once>>
<<declare $day1DidContemplation = false>>
<<declare $day1DidHappyThought = false>>
<<declare $day1DidPushups = false>>
<<endonce>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show Stars>>
<<show Sitting>>
You: I guess I have some time... what should I do?
    -> (contemplate my life on Earth) <<if $day1DidContemplation == false>>
        <<set $day1DidContemplation = true>>
        I ponder the vastness of existence and my place within it.
        The silence of space seems to amplify my thoughts, making me feel both insignificant and connected to the universe.
        -> (hone in on the positive)
            I think back to the nights Dad and I would sit on the porch, staring up at the sky.
            He'd point out constellations and tell me about the astronauts who came before us. He made space sound like a promise.
            That's part of why I'm out here. Not just for the mission. For him.
            <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
            The memory gives me <color=\#88FF88>a quiet sense of purpose</color>.
        -> (dwell on the negative)
            I think back about a time I felt insignificant on Earth.
            Ever since I dropped out of college, I've felt like a disappointment to my family.
            I took the first contract that would launch me off-planet, telling myself distance would make it easier to breathe.
            <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
            I scoff at the concept of unconditional love. In doing so, I <color=\#FF8888>feel sadder</color>, overwhelmed by the vast emptiness around me.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay1>>
    -> (think of something happy) <<if $day1DidHappyThought == false>>
        <<set $day1DidHappyThought = true>>
        I think back to my time on Earth, recalling when my mother taught me how to bake cookies.
        She doesn't show much affection anymore. But the memory still brings a smile to my face.
        She never said she was proud of me. But she let me lick the spoon every time, without asking.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        It's a small comfort in the loneliness of space. I feel <color=\#88FF88>slightly happier</color>.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay1>>
    -> (do some push-ups) <<if $day1DidPushups == false>>
        <<set $day1DidPushups = true>>
        Gh... I was never huge on fitness, but out here, routine is the only thing that keeps the silence from swallowing you whole.
        Each rep feels like a small victory against the emptiness. Fifteen. Sixteen. Seventeen.
        My body still listens to me, even when nothing else does. That has to count for something.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        I feel <color=\#88FF88>a little more grounded</color> afterwards. The burn in my arms is real. That's enough for now.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay1>>
    -> (do my report)
        <<play_sound AlarmClock>>
        A timer goes off in the background.
        You: Sounds like it's time to do my report.
        <<hide_all_objects>>
        <<show PCRoom>>
        <<jump DoJobFirstTime>>
