title: EnterMessage
position: 316,-234
---
I'm frozen in place. Is this really happening?
My mouth doesn't open. I can't speak a word. My voice... is gone.
Out of the hundreds of days I've spent in space, I've never seen something like this.
What should... I... do?
    -> (let the signal through)
        <<jump CatIntro>>
    -> (ignore the signal)
You: ..........
Against my better judgment, I decide to ignore the signal. 
You: Darn static interference...
<<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
I push the signal away, but the guilt lingers.
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<fade_transition 2>>
<<wait 1.5>>
<<play_sound Glitch 0.25>>
<<show_character Cat Obscure right>>
Suddenly, the same signal reappears on the screen. Whatever it is won't take ignorance for an answer.
    -> (let the signal through)
        <<jump CatIntro>>
    -> (unplug the monitor)
        <<hide_all_characters>>
        <<hide MonitorSilhouette>>
        I decide to unplug the monitor, cutting off the signal entirely.
        After a few moments, the screen flickers back to static. I'm alone, again.
        <<jump ForeverAloneNoContact>>
===

title: CatIntro
position: 318,-2
---
My heart is hammering. I can't tell if I'm breathing. There's... something that isn't human. Something that's <i>talking to me</i>.
You: Here goes nothing...
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<play_music CatTheme 0.5>>
<<speed 1>>
???: Hello! See your signal! You okay? You... not hurt?
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
That voice. It's real. This is really happening.
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
???: I hear you. So... you are... <i>human</i>? Real human? From Earth?
    -> ...What?
    -> A cat?
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        ???: Oh! Cat! Those cute things. You say... nice thing? Thank? Thank you!
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        ???: But you okay, yes? You look... alone. Many alone.
            -> I'm... fine.
                <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
                ???: Okay, good. I am... relief? Relieved. Yes.
            -> Not... really.
                <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
                ???: Oh. Space is... lonely place. I know this.
            -> (scream in confusion)
                <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
                I can't help it... I take a deep breath, and...
                You: AAAAAAHHHHHHHH!!!
                <<negative_indicator Cat>>
                <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
                <<show_character Cat Surprised right>>
                The creature on the monitor flinches back, ears flattening.
                <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
                ???: AH! So loud! My ears... they very sensitive!
                <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
                ???: Please... next time more quiet? I not mean scare you...
    -> ...
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
I'm still reeling. An alien, asking if I'm okay. My hands are shaking.
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
???: You not look in danger. So... what you do in space? Why you here?
    -> I'm on a mission. Exploring.
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        ???: Mission? Explore? You go far from home just to... look? That sound lonely.
    -> It's... complicated.
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        ???: Complicated. Yes. I understand this word. Many thing in life is complicated.
    -> Why do you want to know?
        <<negative_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        ???: Sorry. I just... want know. I only small... two orbit old? So many thing I not understand yet.
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
???: Oh! You ping back! I so happy! I send many signal... TEST, HELLO, TALK... I not know if you hear.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
???: I watch your ship long time. I learn little bit of your words. I practice and practice.
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
???: But now you here! You respond! This is... this is very good.
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
???: Before more question... you have name? What I call you? Human have this, one word for each? So interesting to me!
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
My mouth is dry. It's asking for my name. It wants to know what to call me. I'm having a conversation with an alien. I'm having a conversation with an <i>alien</i>.
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
???: I want remember you. Please?
    -> I'm {$playerName}.
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catKnowsPlayerName = true>>
        <<set $catThinksPlayerNameIs = $playerName>>
        <<if $playerName == "Dipper">>
            ???: {$playerName}? Like the star? So cute! I like.
        <<else>>
            ???: {$playerName}! I like this sound. Nice to meet, {$playerName}!
        <<endif>>
    -> I don't know you...
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        <<negative_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
        ???: Oh. Okay. I... too fast? Sorry.
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        ???: But for talk... something to call you? Anything okay.
        -> It's {$playerName}.
            ???: {$playerName}. Nice. I remember.
            <<set $catThinksPlayerNameIs = $playerName>>
        -> I don't have a name.
            <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
            ???: No name? How other human call you then?
            <<show_character Cat Flirt right>>
            ???: I call you "Human" maybe. I good at... nickname? Yes.
    -> ...
        ???: Shy? Okay, okay. No problem.
        <<show_character Cat Flirt right>>
        ???: I call you "Human" then. I good at nickname!
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
???: So... you really human, yes? From Earth? I hear story... so many story! I never see one before!
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
I'm still trying to wrap my head around this. It's excited. It's <i>excited</i> to meet a human. Like I'm some kind of... celebrity. Or a rare animal.
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
???: Human have two leg? And thumb? The... the grabby finger? So many thing I want ask!
-> Yeah, it's pretty cool.
    <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
    <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
    <<positive_indicator Cat>>
    ???: Yes! So cool! You must do many thing with hand. I want see someday!
-> No. What?
    <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
    ???: Oh. I sad. I want see trick with thumb...
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
???: I from place... planet? Far from here. Very far. Nice to meet you, {$catThinksPlayerNameIs}!
    -> You're an alien?
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        <<negative_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
        ???: Alien? I... not from your planet. So maybe yes?
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        ???: I from other place. Far away.
        <<show_character Cat Angry right>>
        ???: But "alien" sound... mean? Like I am strange bad thing. I not mean hurt you.
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        ???: Oh, you want call me something? We not have name. I make one for you! I am Gnarp!
        <<set $catName = "Gnarp">>
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        {$catName}: There. Now you can say.
    -> What should I call you? Do you have a name?
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        ???: Name? For me? We... we not have this. One word for one person? My people not do that. We know each other by... by smell, by sound. By who we are.
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        ???: But you have name! So interesting! So I... I make one! For you to say! Yes!
        ???: I am... I am Gnarp! Gnarp! You can call Gnarp!
        <<set $catName = "Gnarp">>
        <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
        {$catName}: I like it! I am Gnarp now!
    -> Meowdy.
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        ???: Meowdy? What is... oh! Greeting! Interesting!
        <<show_character Cat Flirt right>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        ???: Meowdy to you also! I like this word.
        ???: But, what I call? You ask my name? We not have. So I make one! I am Gnarp!
        <<set $catName = "Gnarp">>
        {$catName}: Yes. Gnarp. For you to say.
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: Oh! One more thing. I... I watch you. Long time. I listen. Your ship, your... talking to yourself? Your reports? I learn little bit of your words. Your English.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: Is not perfect, I know. Sorry. But I try. I want to say hello proper when I finally call.
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: So! You careful here. Space is... dangerous. Many danger.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: Why you here? Why not stay on Earth? Your home?
    -> Escaping it all, I guess.
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        {$catName}: I understand. Sometimes... need get away. I understand.
    -> Exploring the cosmos.
        <<negative_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: Oh. You risk life for... look at space? So brave. Maybe little... crazy? Too.
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
    -> I'm... not sure.
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        {$catName}: Okay. Not sure okay. Sometime we not know. But find safe place good idea. Here very... unpredictable.
<<show_character Cat Surprised right>>
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
A sound from their end... scuffling, something heavy shifting. A low voice, muffled and indistinct, in the background. {$catName} glances off-screen, ears flattening.
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
{$catName}: Oh. I... I sorry. I have to go. Now. Sorry!
<<if $catLikesYou >= $catDislikesYou>>
    <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
    {$catName}: But... you ping me, yes? I want talk again, {$catThinksPlayerNameIs}. Sorry, sorry!
    <<show_character Cat Surprised right>>
    {$catName}: I go. Bye!
<<else>>
    <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
    {$catName}: You take care, {$catThinksPlayerNameIs}. Sorry.
<<endif>>
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
More shuffling. The feed flickers. {$catName} opens their mouth as if to say something else... then the screen cuts to static.
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<hide MonitorSilhouette>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
<<play_music MainTheme>>
The transmission cuts off. Whatever was happening on their end, they're gone.
<<set $charactersSecured += 1>>
Your device receives a strange series of pings afterwards, and the screen flickers back to static. {$catName} is gone.
<<jump ThinkingAfterCatLeaves>>
===

title: ThinkingAfterCatLeaves
position: 310,187
---
<<fade_transition 2>>
<<wait 1>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show Stars>>
<<show Sitting>>
I sit back down... trying to process the encounter I just had.
Who was that creature? How is that even possible?
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
    <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
    Strangely enough, I enjoyed the encounter with them. They seemed... friendly.
    What would it be like for me to have a friend like that?
    I wonder if I'll ever see them again.
<<else>>
    <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
    To me, the whole encounter felt off. Aliens? Of all times, why now?
    I think about what others on Earth would say if they found out about this encounter. Although it is my job to report such things, would they really believe I met a friendly animal alien?
<<endif>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show PCRoom>>
The cabin falls silent again as the static fades back into the background hum.
First contact. That's the kind of thing you're supposed to flag immediately... protocol, duty, all of it.
But my mind is too hazy to think about writing right now.
<<fade_transition 2>>
<<wait 1>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show Stars>>
<<show Sitting>>
I sit with that for a while. The stars don't answer.
I heat up rations. I stare at the same metal walls. The routine carries me through the rest of the evening, but my head is somewhere else. Somewhere between the static and the memory of a voice that wasn't human, asking for my name.
Then, I decide to sleep on it. Just for the meantime.
<<jump VividDream>>
===

title: VividDream
---
<<stop_music>>
<<fade_transition 2>>
<<wait 1>>
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show Stars>>
The stars drift... and I'm no longer in the ship. 
(this part will be more graphic when its not low-fi) I'm in the kitchen, the morning light coming through the window.
My father is at the table, telling my mother he wants to go. An expedition led by NASA. He wants to be one of the explorers.
My mother's face is tight. She keeps shaking her head. He keeps talking.
Then, he turns to me, telling me about a beautiful star. When he goes up, he'll take a picture of it, and one day he'll come back and show it to me in person. He promises.
I believe him. In the dream I still believe him.
    -> (remember my mother's hands on the table)
        My mother's hands are on the table. She doesn't say yes, or no. The light keeps coming through the window.
    -> (remember the way he smiled)
        He's smiling when he says it. Sure. Like it's already decided. The light keeps coming through the window.
<<fade_transition 2>>
<<wait 1>>
(this part will also be more graphic) I'm in elementary school. I proudly tell my friends my dad might go to space. He'll see the stars up close!
Then, the rumors start. "His daddy doesn't love him." I hear it in the hallways, at the lunch table.
    -> (remember their faces)
        Their faces are blurry now. The dream doesn't hold the details. Only the weight of it.
    -> (remember the hallway)
        The hallway stretches. Small chairs. Crayon art on the walls. Someone's laugh, somewhere. Then the dream shifts.
<<fade_transition 2>>
<<wait 1>>
(graphics tbd) Now, I'm in middle school.
One day he was there. The next, he wasn't. The house was quieter. My mother stopped talking about him the way she used to. 
I told myself he was in space. That he was on the expedition. That he was keeping his promise.
My classmates looked at me differently now. Pity. They'd touch my shoulder. You're okay, right?
Everyone trying to comfort me... for something I didn't believe. I didn't want their pity. I stopped trying to explain. 
I didn't make friends after that. Not really. I had people I sat with. Nobody I trusted.
    -> (look at the stars)
        The stars are still there. The same ones. The one he loved, visible from everywhere. I never got the picture.
    -> (let the dream fade)
        The dream doesn't fade instantly, but it gets hazier. Somewhere, I'm still that kid in the kitchen, believing him.
<<jump EndDay1>>
===

